\section{Derived test fixtures}{

A few further bundled objects are derived from ex3 and kept under their
historical names; they are not part of the ex1--ex7 scheme and exist for
regression testing: \code{inc_sub10_rep_classic}, \code{inc_sub10_rep_mean},
\code{inc_sub10_rep_end}, \code{inc_sub10_rep_trans} (increment reference results),
\code{processed_pulled_sub10}, \code{processed_heights_nfi_sub10} and
\code{processed_heights_bav_sub10} (intermediate tree-preparation results).
}

\section{Note on the Format-2 example (ex2)}{

ex2 currently provides only the tree and inventory-point tables. A Format-2
dead-wood table (the "07" sheet) and a regeneration table are not bundled yet;
they can be added later.
}

\section{Stand register (Revierbuch)}{

Besides the raw -> pre -> fe_inventory chain, FeNEU offers a separate strand
that produces a \strong{stand register} (\emph{Revierbuch}) from the inventory input
data. It needs stand-level attributes that an \code{fe_inventory} object does not
carry. For stand-wise inventories these are read from a metadata file with
\code{\link[=import_standwise_relascope_format1_metadata]{import_standwise_relascope_format1_metadata()}};
\code{\link[=import_standwise_relascope_format1_stand_register_bundle]{import_standwise_relascope_format1_stand_register_bundle()}} orchestrates
trees and metadata for \code{\link[=stand_register_pdf]{stand_register_pdf()}}. Set \strong{ex6} bundles such a
metadata file (\code{stand_metadata.txt}) as an example; the three processing
stages above never touch it.
}

